+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, Narrowing by Specialty Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable records. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Whether it was deliberately declined was never recorded.
+
+A request to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty collided with the row as written. The owner decided the collision at intake (2026-09-30): "free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Rejected by the owner: narrowing the directory by a specialty it already shows adds no new search pattern.
+2. **Remove NG-9 for veterinarians.** Rejected by the owner: free-text veterinarian search would repeat the owner search the sample already demonstrates.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search and pet and visit search stay declined. Narrowing the directory by a shown specialty is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 declines searching for a pet or a visit, and free-text search for a veterinarian. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by a specialty it already shows is a requirement, not a non-goal.
+
+The narrowing adds no on-page control; a visible control needs its own owner request. Pet and visit search keep their original, unconfirmed provenance.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The veterinarian directory gains a narrowing capability on both its paged and its machine-readable forms.
+- A request for free-text veterinarian search still collides with NG-9 and proceeds only on a recorded owner decision.
+- A request to narrow the directory by an attribute it does not show falls outside this decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the narrowing requirement.
